# net-fs/cifs-utils ships mount.cifs (packages.list). Its default-on +acl/+ads
# hard-RDEPEND >=net-fs/samba, and samba cannot be cross-built here: its waf
# configure runs the BUILD host's perl and requires Parse::Yapp::Driver, but
# net-fs/samba lists dev-perl/Parse-Yapp in DEPEND (not BDEPEND), so under the
# cross layout it merges into the SYSROOT only and the host perl never has it:
#     perl module Parse::Yapp::Driver 1.05 : not found
#     ERROR: net-fs/samba-4.24.7::gentoo failed (configure phase)
# cifs-utils is then dropped under --keep-going and the requested-atom completeness
# gate fails the whole La Frite light-desktop build (prover B, 2026-11-10, ~3h45m in).
#
# Same answer as specs-rpi5/ and specs-jetson/portage/package.use/cifs: acl only
# adds the cifsacl/cifsidmap helpers and ads adds AD/Kerberos, neither used on this
# desktop; dropping both removes the samba + krb5 + ngtcp2 chain, and mount.cifs is
# still built and installed.
net-fs/cifs-utils -acl -ads
